rota lap 5330, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; read follow-our-compass, the Lindy effect and the long return, and the grain and the crossing. Listening for the page nobody answered pointed at REDS %589's booked remainder, whose whole recorded reason was the word cannot.
think My lane's three open reds all want Keaton's word -- %807's head insert is a ruling about how places are assigned, %767's four derivations change what the product admits, %765's 41 record families are a molt. So the lap went to a booked remainder instead.
think %589 closed its shipped instance on 20260908 and left one copy: rye/tests/mantra_weave_test.rye inlines a three-field Line, Diff and Weave, standing under mantra_weave_model's DISAGREE_CEILING=1. The archive says only that it cannot import the module.
think A bare cannot is a sentence no next hand can start from, so the lap ran it. Four readings on metal. Zig refuses @import("../../mantra/src/weave.rye") outright, error: import of file outside module path.
think A renamed symlink beside a test DOES work for a module importing only std -- mantra_weave.rye pointing at mantra/src/weave.rye compiled, and Weave.apply and current ran through it in a throwaway pen.
think It does not reach mantra/src/diff.rye, which holds the LCS half. That module imports weave.rye by bare name, and the rye bridge resolves a symlinked module's own imports relative to the symlink's directory -- it asked for weave.rye beside the symlink and read FileNotFound.
think rye_harness_roster_scan.sh enumerates that room with -type f -o -type l and gates files_unlisted at zero, so a symlink there reds a standing guard until parity_ch01.rish names its stem, and a named stem is one the harness tries to run over a module carrying no main.
obs So the block is the parity corpus admitting no module beside its tests, which is a ruling about rye/ rather than about mantra/. Nothing in this lane opens it; the four doors are named where the next hand reads them.
obs What needed no word was the file's own head. It said it exercises the pure core of Mantra and that its model was inlined from mantra/src/main.rye. Both went false on 20260908.151057, when main.rye began importing weave.rye and stopped declaring the three types.
obs A test that inlines its subject passes forever and its passing is evidence about nothing -- %449 taught that in this same file's room, and the head was still telling a reader the opposite.
obs The one em dash the file carried went to -- on touch, so TRAIL_CEILING fell 1307 to 1306 in tools/fixtures/r/rye_comment_ascii_scan.sh, with its own arc row written beside the three before it.
obs The claim was opened, committed and pushed before any byte moved, and its rebase onto xy conflicted on the claim board; the resolution was diffed against xy/main and reads exactly upstream plus one row, so no peer's closed claim came back.
file rye/tests/mantra_weave_test.rye the head now names what the file tests, says the snapshot is three fields behind, and carries the four measured readings and their doors
file tools/fixtures/r/rye_comment_ascii_scan.sh TRAIL_CEILING 1307 to 1306 with its arc row, because the ceiling only falls and a lap that converts lowers it
